ng questions.\n\n## REQUIREMENT\n\n# Animation Is Data Visualization Not Decoration\n\n## Metadata\n- **Category**: functionality\n- **Effort**: Unknown (N/A/3)\n- **Impact**: Unknown (N/A/3)\n- **Scan Type**: insight_synth\n- **Generated**: 1/30/2026, 1:23:57 AM\n\n## Description\nAnimatedNumber and AnimatedProgressRing animate values to show change. Extend this concept: all data displays should animate when data changes to help users track what changed. Create an AnimatedValue primitive that wraps any changing value with configurable transition visualization.\n\n## Reasoning\nAnimation in data-heavy interfaces serves a cognitive purpose - it directs attention to what changed. Currently animation is used sporadically. Making animation-on-change systematic would improve comprehension of evolving research data.\n\n## Context\n\n**Note**: This section provides supporting architectural documentation and is NOT a hard requirement. Use it as guidance to understand existing code structure and maintain consistency.\n\n### Context: Report Theming & Cards\n\n**Description**: Themed UI components for reports: stat cards, sections, badges, and core elements. Includes animated numbers and theme context for consistent styling.\n**Related Files**:\n- `src/components/report/ThemedCards.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/core/ThemeContext.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/core/AnimatedNumber.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/core/index.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/shared/Cards.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/shared/Badges.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/shared/ProgressBar.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/shared/Icons.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/shared/index.tsx`\n\n**Post-Implementation**: After completing this requirement, evaluate if the context description or file paths need updates. Use the appropriate API/DB query to update the context if architectural changes were made.\n\n## Recommended Skills\n\nUse Claude Code skills as appropriate for implementation guidance. Check `.claude/skills